# ===== 2. VIOLATIONS FOUND AND FIXED =====
# The first real run (before any app/ change) found 0 violations on all 14 scans. axe also reports 'incomplete' (needs review) results;
# a temporary probe (console.log of violations / passes / incomplete per scan, reverted) showed, on /perfil/<seller>:
#   AXE-INCOMPLETE aria-prohibited-attr p[aria-label="4,5 de 5"] :: <p aria-label="4,5 de 5"><span class="price">4,5</span> <span aria-hidden="true">★★★★★</span></p> :: 
#   AXE-INCOMPLETE color-contrast p[aria-label="4,5 de 5"] > span[aria-hidden="true"] :: <span aria-hidden="true">★★★★★</span> :: Element content contains only non-text characters
#   AXE-INCOMPLETE color-contrast li[aria-label="5 de 5"] > p:nth-child(1) > span[aria-hidden="true"] :: <span aria-hidden="true">★★★★★</span> :: Element content contains only non-text characters
#   AXE-INCOMPLETE color-contrast li[aria-label="4 de 5"] > p:nth-child(1) > span[aria-hidden="true"] :: <span aria-hidden="true">★★★★☆</span> :: Element content contains only non-text characters
# Fixed: aria-prohibited-attr. A <p> (role paragraph) may not carry aria-label (ARIA 1.2), so a screen reader could drop 'de 5' from
#   the average. app/perfil/[userId]/page.tsx now wraps the average and its stars in <span role="img" aria-label="4,5 de 5">; the look
#   is unchanged and SellerProfilePage.average('4,5 de 5') still finds it by label. Rules passed on that page: 22 -> 24.
# Not a defect: color-contrast 'incomplete' x3 on the aria-hidden star glyphs (axe cannot rate symbol-only text; they are
#   --ink-primary #0F1B2D on #FFFFFF, far above 4.5:1). Left to the manual contrast audit at launch.
#
